# Third-party notices

## MSA Sans (src/ui/fonts/)

The UI typeface is a subset of **Gowun Dodum** (고운돋움) by Yanghee Ryu (류양희),
licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. The full licence text is in
`src/ui/fonts/OFL.txt`, and the copyright and licence records are preserved
inside the font binary itself.

- Upstream: https://github.com/yangheeryu/Gowun-Dodum
- Distributed via: https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/gowundodum
- Version subsetted: 2.000
- Presented as "MSA Sans". Gowun Dodum declares **no** Reserved Font Name, so
  OFL 1.1 §3 does not require the rename; it is a project convention, so that a
  packaged build and a machine with the font already installed resolve to the
  same metrics under the same family name. The copyright (name ID 0), licence
  (13) and licence URL (14) records are carried through unchanged, and the
  unique-ID record names what this file actually is.

### It was Pretendard, and why it is not

The previous typeface was a subset of Pretendard by Kil Hyung-jin (길형진), also
OFL 1.1, in two weights. That choice was made for the art direction before this
one: a Korean-first humanist sans with a wide weight axis, as the nearest voice
to the Frutiger family the aero look is usually described with.

The current direction asks for the opposite of a wide axis — the display voice
is DRAWN (`src/ui/lettering.js`) and the face is left with the quiet, small,
precise half of the work. Gowun Dodum is a single weight with open counters and
slightly modulated strokes, which is that half.

### What was kept

| range | why |
|---|---|
| `U+AC00–D7A3` | Every precomposed Hangul syllable, all 11172 — verified present in the source and in the subset. Non-negotiable: nicknames are user input and `NICKNAME_RE` admits the whole block, so a narrower subset renders somebody's name as tofu — a bug that surfaces for one user on one device. |
| `U+3130–318F` | Hangul compatibility jamo. 94 of the 96 are present; the two absent are archaic letters the source font does not have either. Every letter an IME actually emits (`U+3131–3163`) is there. |
| `U+0020–007E`, `U+00A0–00FF` | Latin and Latin-1, complete. |
| `U+2010–2027`, `U+2030–205E` | Punctuation — dashes, ellipsis, the middle dot the UI uses as a separator. |
| `U+2190–2193` | Arrows. |

`U+1100–11FF` (conjoining jamo) is **absent from the source font** — Gowun Dodum
2.000 carries 0 of those 256 codepoints, exactly as Pretendard did. Asking for it
would be a silent no-op. Korean IME composition on the platforms this ships to
produces compatibility jamo and precomposed syllables, both of which are covered.

### What was dropped

Vietnamese and Latin Extended beyond Latin-1, and the punctuation outside the two
ranges above. The source is a 7.2 MB TTF whose weight is almost entirely the
Hangul, so the subset is 387 KB rather than the tenfold cut the previous font's
notice describes — there was much less to remove.

### Weights

**One static face, 400.** Not two, and not a variable font.

`src/core/tokens.js` exports `FONT_WEIGHTS = [400]` and throws at module load if
any `TYPE` entry names a weight that is not in it. `src/ui/styles.css` declares
exactly one `@font-face`. Both are deliberate: a `font-weight: 700` that the
browser cannot resolve is not a slightly-off weight, it is a SYNTHESISED one —
the outlines are smeared, canvas 2D bakes that smear into a texture where it
cannot be undone, and different engines smear by different amounts.
